Hello,

Recently I asked for help on LaTeX-L to work on l3doc, and received an  
offer by one Arno Trautmann. He's fairly new to the expl3 code (as was  
I when I started) but he seems enthusiastic to help for now.

I have the idea to set up an external version control repository  
(probably at GitHub) with a copy of l3doc (only!) to encourage him to  
work on it; as per the intentions of the LPPL I'd call it "l3doc-dev"  
or something like that. I'd work on it with him and merge changes back  
into the official SVN repository.

However, I recognise that this idea might be a little controversial,  
so that's all it is at the moment -- an idea. What do you think?

Will

